  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water, Energy, and Food resources-Nexus (WEF-Nexus) in the agriculture and foodsector, Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Santa Eulalia river sub-basin in Peru provides 50% of the water needs and 70% of the electricity needs of metropolitan Lima. Moreover, the basin produces a wide variety of fruits (custard apples and avocados) and vegetables that are sold in Lima.Climatic variability compounded by climate change results in decreased availability of and access to natural resources (mainly water and food). This affects local populations directly and metropolitan Lima indirectly.The Netherlands Government supports the Peruvian Government in integrating WEF-nexus (Water, Energy and Food resources) aspects in its sustainable development and climate change policies in which water, energy and agri&amp;food are integrated.The Peru Nexus project will result in more efficient use of water, energy and food resources, enhanced resilience to the impact of climate change, improved agricultural practices and the development of the local private sector in the Santa Eulalia river sub-basin.</narrative>
  </description>
